    "done_when": "In imas_ambix/agent/telemetry_retention.py compare_tiers no longer builds a TelemetryIndex. It reads raw, minute and hour rows, buckets them by UTC hour, and compares telemetry_store's partitioned totals of engine.generation_tokens, engine.prompt_tokens and engine.uncached_prompt_tokens per hour and counter, giving the same verdicts as before. A counter absent from every row of a tier in an hour is reported as absent, not as zero; a tier holding a value where raw holds none is a failure. Tests in tests/test_telemetry_retention.py keep every existing verdict test passing; add one asserting the absent-versus-zero rule; add one asserting the check over a synthetic raw file of 20,000 rows and its compactions completes in under 10 s. The manifest reports, for the real raw file /work/projects/imas_gpu/agents/receipts/deepseek-v4-1-flash-1271709.jsonl and its staged tiers in /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/imas-ambix/0c4316b2-553f-4a0a-ae02-c42d88de747c/srw-rebuild-tiers-from-raw-staged/tiers/ (read-only), what raw, minute and hour each hold for engine.generation_tokens in hour 2026-09-15T19:00Z: absent, null, or the number. The worker writes nothing under /work/projects/imas_gpu/agents/receipts. Gate: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_telemetry_retention.py tests/test_telemetry_compaction_runs.py passes, pytest tests/test_agent_serve_registry.py -k agent_package_modules_parse_with_serving_python passes, uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0; the gate log's first line names the commit it ran at and each command's exit status is recorded as EXIT=0 or the non-zero status; any evidence fragment written ends with a trailing newline",
